{"id":"668d7e295278eaa5","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-thm-perfect-cardinality.md","title":"Perfect Set Cardinality","display":"thm-perfect-cardinality — Perfect Set Cardinality","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-perfect-cardinality","aliases":["58-thm-perfect-cardinality"],"display":"thm-perfect-cardinality — Perfect Set Cardinality","depends_on":["[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-perfect-cardinality"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-perfect-cardinality</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-perfect-cardinality — Perfect Set Cardinality"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md\">../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" href=\"?note=f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md\">../batch08/58-df-perfect.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0b8de0824384672e\" href=\"?note=0b8de0824384672e\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md\">../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}\">\\(P \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}\\)</span> (subset of the reals, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d_{\\mathbb R}(x,y)=|x-y|\">\\(d_{\\mathbb R}(x,y)=|x-y|\\)</span> (the usual metric on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\">\\(\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\)</span> (perfect-set predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" href=\"?note=f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md\">../batch08/58-df-perfect.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P \\neq \\emptyset\">\\(P \\neq \\emptyset\\)</span> (nonempty set, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"0b8de0824384672e\" href=\"?note=0b8de0824384672e\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md\">../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}perfect\\text{-}cardinality}\\vdash\n\\forall P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land P\\neq\\varnothing\\Bigr)\n\\to\n|P|=2^{\\aleph_0}=\\mathfrak c\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}perfect\\text{-}cardinality}\\vdash\n\\forall P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land P\\neq\\varnothing\\Bigr)\n\\to\n|P|=2^{\\aleph_0}=\\mathfrak c\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A binary splitting construction inside <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span> gives an injection <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2^\\omega\\hookrightarrow P\">\\(2^\\omega\\hookrightarrow P\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The reverse inequality follows from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\">\\(P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\)</span>, so Cantor–Bernstein gives equality.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md","status":"resolved","id":"f6afc84fe5b2b44e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md","status":"resolved","id":"0b8de0824384672e","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-emptyset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md","status":"resolved","id":"535817bf563314f5","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$P \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ (subset of the reals, see [[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md","status":"resolved","id":"f6afc84fe5b2b44e","anch